  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>The formula to calculate the de Broglie wavelength of a particle is given by</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>h</mi><msqrt><mn>2</mn><mi>m</mi><mi>K</mi></msqrt></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>Now, the masses of the given particles are interrelated by the following relations:</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtable columnalign=\"right center left\" columnspacing=\"0px\"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>e</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><mo>&#8776;</mo></mtd><mtd><mfrac><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mn>1837</mn></mfrac></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>&#945;</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mn>4</mn><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>p</mi></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable></math></p><p>The de Broglie wavelength for electron is given by</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtable columnspacing=\"0px\" columnalign=\"right center left\"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mi>e</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mfrac><mi>h</mi><msqrt><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><mfenced><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>K</mi></mrow></mfenced></msqrt></mfrac></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd/><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mfrac><mi>h</mi><msqrt><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mn>8</mn><mn>1837</mn></mfrac></mstyle><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mi>K</mi></msqrt></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></math></p><p>The de Broglie wavelength for proton is given by</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtable columnspacing=\"0px\" columnalign=\"right center left\"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mi>p</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mfrac><mi>h</mi><msqrt><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>K</mi></mrow></mfenced></msqrt></mfrac></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd/><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mfrac><mi>h</mi><msqrt><mn>4</mn><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mi>K</mi></msqrt></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>3</mn></mfenced></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></math></p><p>And, the de Broglie wavelength of alpha particle is given by</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtable columnspacing=\"0px\" columnalign=\"right center left\"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mi>&#945;</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mfrac><mi>h</mi><msqrt><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>&#945;</mi></msub><mi>K</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd/><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mo>&#160;</mo><mfrac><mi>h</mi><msqrt><mn>2</mn><mfenced><mrow><mn>4</mn><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>p</mi></msub></mrow></mfenced><mi>K</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd/><mtd><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mfrac><mi>h</mi><msqrt><mn>8</mn><msub><mi>m</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mi>K</mi></msqrt></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>4</mn></mfenced></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></math></p><p>From equation (2), (3) and (4), it can be concluded that&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mi>e</mi></msub><mo>&#62;</mo><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo>&#62;</mo><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mi>&#945;</mi></msub></math>.</p></blockquote>",
